MacOSX arm64 (Apple Silicon)

-	Default emu is Cocoa (`emu-cocoa`), installed as `MacOSX/arm64/bin/emu`
-	JIT is on by default (`cflag=1`); use `-c0` for the interpreter
-	arm64 JIT: IMCALL/IMFRAME/IINDC inlined; `das` for `-c4+`; mmap freed on unload
-	User is `inferno` unless `/usr/<host-login>` exists under the Inferno root
-	Default window 1024×768 (`-gWxH` to override); window is resizable
-	Resize keeps softscreen fixed and scales the blit (aspect locked)
-	Fullscreen: View → Enter Full Screen (⌃⌘F)
-	`#A` audio via CoreAudio (`/dev/audio`, `/dev/audioctl`)
-	IPv6 dual-stack (`ipif6-posix`)
-	Console-only build: `mk CONF=emu-g install` → `emu-g` only (does not replace `emu`)

Try:
	emu wm/wm
	emu -c0 wm/wm		# interpreter
	emu -g1280x800 wm/wm

Notes:
-	Fresh binaries are ad-hoc codesigned on install (needed on modern macOS)
-	1 Inferno pixel = 1 point; Retina uses layer contentsScale for sharp upscale
-	FP exception traps are left off (Apple Silicon + host frameworks)
-	386/power: Carbon `win.c`; `mkfile-x11` uses X11
-	Host CFLAGS use `-O2` (`mkfiles/mkfile-MacOSX-arm64`)
-	`libmemdraw` load/unload/line must use `sizeof(u32)` for `Memimage.width`
	strides (not `sizeof(ulong)`); on LP64 the wrong stride smashed the image
	pool and crashed `wm/colors` in `flushimage`
